#N canvas 20 20 1660 1280 12;
#X text 20 20 u_map -- THE MAP \, and the only file in Cut It that says what a control MEANS. Every device below publishes named controls onto param and stops there \; everything above is driven by the buses this file writes. Nothing in e_ or c_ may ever learn that a nanoKONTROL exists \, and this is the layer that keeps that true., f 58;
#X text 20 150 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 200 THE WHOLE MAP \, IN WORDS -- keep this in step with the route box below. og-knob-1 \, the Organelle's knob 1 \, is master tempo over 10 to 500 BPM. og-aux \, the Organelle's aux button \, toggles the transport. That is all of it: 42 other controls are published and mapped to nothing \, which is the normal state of affairs., f 58;
#X obj 20 380 r param;
#X obj 20 430 route og-knob-1 og-aux;
#X obj 20 510 * 490;
#X obj 20 550 + 10;
#X obj 20 590 + 0.5;
#X obj 20 630 i;
#X obj 20 690 s tempo;
#X obj 400 510 t b;
#X obj 400 560 f;
#X obj 400 610 select 0 1;
#X obj 400 680 s start;
#X obj 560 680 s stop;
#X obj 760 380 r start;
#X msg 760 430 1;
#X obj 960 380 r stop;
#X msg 960 430 0;
#X text 20 760 ONE BRANCH PER MAPPING \, AND DELIBERATELY NOT A TABLE. A text lookup driving a dynamic send could write ANY global name with no evidence of it anywhere on the canvas \, which quietly defeats an allowlist the whole project audits by reading. Here the set of things a control can reach is the set of s boxes you can see. Revisit when the count passes about ten -- plan-v02.md defers that to v0.3., f 58;
#X text 20 900 ROUNDING BELONGS HERE \, NOT IN u_tempo. A control's range is this file's decision \; the LEGAL range is u_tempo's \, and it clamps at 5 to 600 -- WIDER at both ends \, so a bench \, a tap tempo or an LFO is not limited by what one knob chose. It also means this knob cannot itself provoke an out-of-range warning \, which is the right way round. + 0.5 then i is a round rather than a truncate \, and it is what stops the footer flickering between 119.7 and 120.1., f 58;
#X text 20 1070 route's REJECT IS EVERY UNMAPPED CONTROL \, and it goes nowhere on purpose. Unmapped is the normal state of 42 controls \, so warning about it would be noise \, not information. This is also where an r mode would gate the branches when something finally drives that bus -- the shape does not have to change for that., f 58;
#X text 700 510 THE TOGGLE HOLDS NO STATE OF ITS OWN. It reads back what actually HAPPENED \, from whoever caused it \, so a start from the bench or from Phase 6 cannot leave the button pressing the wrong way. Pd is synchronous \, so the s start below updates this f during the send and returns before the press has finished -- close \, but not a loop., f 44;
#X text 700 700 select 0 1 GIVES BANGS \, one per state \, and its reject cannot fire because the store only ever holds 0 or 1. Nothing hangs off it \, which is the safe way to treat a reject that carries data., f 44;
#X text 700 850 og-aux ARRIVES AS A FLOAT. route strips the selector \, and a remainder that is a lone 1 really is a float -- so this branch needs a t b in front of the store \, exactly like every other place in this repo where something behind an outlet expects a bang and gets a value., f 44;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 4 1 10 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 12 1 14 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 11 1;
#X connect 17 0 18 0;
#X connect 18 0 11 1;
